 75GE    74GE(A,2P1NG):XUNDL-6         2018NI04                           201807
 75GE c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2018Ni04:                          
 75GE2c  Phys Rev C 97, 034322 (2018)                                           
 75GE c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU), March 23, 2018                        
 75GE c  2018Ni04: E=58.6-62.6 MeV alpha beams were produced from the Separated 
 75GE2c  Sector Cyclotron of iThemba LABS in South Africa. Target was a 2.85    
 75GE3c  mg/cm{+2} {+74}Ge metallic foil on a 10.8 mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. |g 
 75GE4c  rays were detected with the AFRODITE array consisting of 8             
 75GE5c  Compton-suppressed clover detectors and 2 low-energy photon            
 75GE6c  spectrometers. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g|g|g-coin,              
 75GE7c  |g|g(|q)(ADO). Deduced levels, J, |p, band structures, |g-ray          
 75GE8c  multipolarities. Comparisons with triaxial-particle-rotor model        
 75GE9c  calculations.                                                          
 75GE cG M$Deduced from ADO ratios. ADO ratio is defined as                     
 75GE2cG R{-ADO}=I|g(135|')/I|g(90|') and typical values are |J1.2 for stretched
 75GE3cG quadrupole transition and |J0.8 for stretched dipole (2018Ni04)        
 75GE cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies (by compiler), assuming  
 75GE2cL |DE|g=0.5 keV.                                                         
 75GE cL J$As given in 2018Ni04, based on |g|g(|q)(ADO) and known spin-parities 
 75GE2cL for low-lying states                                                   
 75GE cL T$From Adopted Levels of {+75}Ge in ENSDF database.                    
 75GE cL SEQ(A)$Sequence 1                                                      
 75GE cL SEQ(B)$Sequence 2                                                      
 75GE cL SEQ(C)$Sequence 3                                                      
